{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:01:02.238884Z","id":"1e865f5898417badd327885effd8f23704d974c60b8e030590ab54c32f190710","body":{"detail":"ContainerWorkspace::propose (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs:289) waits preview_timeout_secs once, then records the fix with verify_url null; nothing returns to it. A claxbot/ branch deploys only after a person adds preview-approved, so unless that and the deploy both land inside the wait the reporter gets no address to verify at. Raising the timeout is bounded by max_run_minutes (30 by default, crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:129). Closing this takes a step that records verify_url once the preview serves the commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"61b4f73901941bb4d0f034c10383c28e78897ad709e579a2628f24cfc58519da"},"summary":"With the approval gate, ClaxBot usually reports a Clax fix with no verify_url, and a later preview reaches nobody","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/changelist.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:01:02.238905Z","id":"05dc0d89df42d726f6886b686a7c90825fb5fc265caef9f3ad990b0ee8f487ef","body":{"detail":"Neither repository's preview workflow has the gate of .github/workflows/preview.yml. Changelist's README says its preview credentials equal production deploy access until previews have their own Fly organization and Neon project; Pathbase's previews run in the environment its dev deploy uses. Both profiles are examples only until that changes. The headers of deploy/claxbot-workspace/changelist.toml and pathbase.toml say so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":8},"content_hash":"0fab6ddaf9d92c2bacde998479c93d8cb7d9b42bd70c4561bf16fbf4885f2fae"},"summary":"Changelist and Pathbase deploy any repository branch with unreviewed code holding credentials, so these profiles must stay off until those repositories gate claxbot/ branches","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/changelist.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:01:02.238922Z","id":"5386e62a1e5a649a46456f1c3fa0bd348fe0705b0b1ba2fe4ab64e46581ea1ff","body":{"detail":"Preview::ready (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/preview.rs) then accepts any 200. Neither health route names a commit, and both builds check out the merge commit, so a stamp from the build's own checkout would not match the head ClaxBot compares. On a later propose to the same pull request verify_url points at a preview without the fix. deploy/claxbot-workspace/pathbase.toml:74-81 has the same comment. The fix is in those repositories: the head's full SHA in the health answer.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"5c23e282eed1bfb2f4b5ea21df0731acbb5964f94391ce54b0181080edc085bb"},"summary":"preview_names_commit is false for Changelist and Pathbase, so a second push's wait ends at once on the previous deployment","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:01:02.238943Z","id":"74fba32562c460b48e4109133ad9091dccd300cb2d75061c8484a0be000f41f2","body":{"detail":"TargetConfig::open (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs) reads write_token_env and read_token_env when the workspace opens, and keeps them. An installation token lasts an hour, and nothing mints one, so a read token is neither per run nor short-lived in practice unless the daemon restarts, and a fine-grained personal token is the only long-lived choice. Closing this takes something that mints per run from the App's key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"4fe6345c3a13fdb3d10b5e77f8c93edccae35220d0bc2a3542cb61c1464320d6"},"summary":"Tokens are read once at open, so GitHub App installation tokens expire under a running daemon","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:19:40.130370Z","id":"f9afbbd84adef752f9a6b6e9ab21c65014b31a81383729283d67bfbbdcf48ab3","body":{"detail":"ContainerWorkspace::propose (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs:289) waits preview_timeout_secs once, then records the fix with verify_url null; nothing returns to it. ClaxBot's pull request deploys only after a person comments /preview with the head's SHA, so unless that and the deploy both land inside the wait the reporter gets no address to verify at. Raising the timeout is bounded by max_run_minutes (30 by default, crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:129). Closing this takes a step that records verify_url once the preview serves the commit.\n\nRe-anchored after the lines moved; originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"c7e08ce88f6dcff0e26f43ce018713747ef2e480540a546915f832e8eb90272a"},"summary":"With the approval gate, ClaxBot usually reports a Clax fix with no verify_url, and a later preview reaches nobody","supersedes":"1e865f5898417badd327885effd8f23704d974c60b8e030590ab54c32f190710","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/changelist.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:19:40.282192Z","id":"4da9fcf0df31ed074c3dcac3a5b2f99da7bf667c3be33de3f798b36b1edcb7dc","body":{"detail":"Preview::ready (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/preview.rs) then accepts any 200. Neither health route names a commit, and both builds check out the merge commit, so a stamp from the build's own checkout would not match the head ClaxBot compares. On a later propose to the same pull request verify_url points at a preview without the fix. deploy/claxbot-workspace/pathbase.toml:80-87 has the same comment. The fix is in those repositories: the head's full SHA in the health answer.\n\nRe-anchored after the lines moved; originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"5c23e282eed1bfb2f4b5ea21df0731acbb5964f94391ce54b0181080edc085bb"},"summary":"preview_names_commit is false for Changelist and Pathbase, so a second push's wait ends at once on the previous deployment","supersedes":"5386e62a1e5a649a46456f1c3fa0bd348fe0705b0b1ba2fe4ab64e46581ea1ff","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:19:40.435395Z","id":"384a704732a4437d6784db2c1e701c099ce53b88f38e474bde0a537a01e02951","body":{"detail":"TargetConfig::open (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs) reads write_token_env and read_token_env when the workspace opens, and keeps them. An installation token lasts an hour, and nothing mints one, so a read token is neither per run nor short-lived in practice unless the daemon restarts, and a fine-grained personal token is the only long-lived choice. Closing this takes something that mints per run from the App's key.\n\nRe-anchored after the lines moved; originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"afed2e20353b2d9b269250daf76617655bb97ccb698ff4947254d3d31a7b8c37"},"summary":"Tokens are read once at open, so GitHub App installation tokens expire under a running daemon","supersedes":"74fba32562c460b48e4109133ad9091dccd300cb2d75061c8484a0be000f41f2","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:34:10.864220Z","id":"190c6d7aa8e995eb3d65bb9f36d4d6033791d535e0bd7ab45751514b2f90643d","body":{"detail":"TargetConfig::open (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs) reads write_token_env and read_token_env when the workspace opens, and keeps them. An installation token lasts an hour, and nothing mints one, so a read token is neither per run nor short-lived in practice unless the daemon restarts, and a fine-grained personal token is the only long-lived choice. Closing this takes something that mints per run from the App's key.\n\nRe-anchored after the lines moved; originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"b1a5efaf0784db9045522f5c5ac18b05018e70014bdf9fc2fc8e1df0ded2dabd"},"summary":"Tokens are read once at open, so GitHub App installation tokens expire under a running daemon","supersedes":"384a704732a4437d6784db2c1e701c099ce53b88f38e474bde0a537a01e02951","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:57:16.723276Z","id":"4617b0d0c06645d9458b2e109d55e6b276e1dd7eff56e8435bfbb7209a293d0f","body":{"detail":"Reports point at the overlay, so a fix usually lands there, which is why writable_paths keeps web/overlay/src/. It is also the code that takes reporter input on every shell page, and a model steered by a report can change it; only a person's review of the pull request stands between. Decide: keep it writable, or protect it and let such reports end in a note for the queue's members.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":74},"content_hash":"efaf85c9c86eb9793882656545583c5628b91ff06bb7f8dfd3cbc7c2af6f04fe"},"summary":"web/overlay/src/ stays writable though the overlay runs on every page of clax.dev","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:57:16.730069Z","id":"3ca2d0b98341010e944b1d4cc2042b7a5175cf2c76c66bc7c6a57382c838c5d4","body":{"detail":"The wait begins at the proposal and a preview here starts only on a person's command, so a review longer than 20 minutes ends in PREVIEW_MISSED and the later preview tells nobody. A longer timeout costs a poll every 10 seconds, detached from the run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":217},"end":{"line":217},"content_hash":"f4c38d2e5cca48cfe6a33d09e883272a149330de0726b0b0690520f0a229018e"},"summary":"preview_timeout_secs of 1200 waits 20 minutes for a person's /preview","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:57:16.731288Z","id":"5243cae383d0f5b444018d742a669882c3b97b698bb9ab7c7deac8fc64cfdc70","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f9afbbd84adef752f9a6b6e9ab21c65014b31a81383729283d67bfbbdcf48ab3","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":217},"content_hash":"fd1fae38eaa16ab61ca45b1518fa37db1ba39154146fb6ba178e1b8052318dd2"},"summary":"The comment above preview_url now says what holds: propose does not wait, a fix is held until the preview is up, the wait outlives the run, and a wait that ends with none tells the queue's members. Proposed for closing by whoever owns it.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:05:45.311457Z","id":"cde8eb1121d3f61b2c5571ba863a9572b33459f800dc0bcf0a11a746657c5e8e","body":{"detail":"Access lets a machine through with CF-Access-Client-Id and CF-Access-Client-Secret under a Service Auth policy, or one configured header holding both as JSON (https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/identity/service-tokens/, read 2026-11-06). outgoing in crates/clax-worker/src/workspace.rs:162 adds only Authorization: Bearer, and grep finds no cf-access in crates/clax-worker/src, crates/clax-bot-remote/src or the service. So with an Access application on the hostname every Worker request stops at Access. Options: (a) add two Worker secrets and send the headers from outgoing, with setup_of treating them as a pair, keeping the bearer as a second factor; (b) accept a public tunnel hostname guarded by the 32-byte bearer alone, which every route checks first, as a waiver. Until then the runbook publishes the hostname with no Access. Cloudflare also says the origin must validate the Access token, or Protect with Access be on in the tunnel, which (a) must include.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":159},"end":{"line":169},"content_hash":"b029d555341def1bee55b5dae6f23cda2e76d208e87f6375cec29b2e61abe276"},"summary":"Cloudflare Access cannot front the workspace service: the Worker sends no service token","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/service.Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:05:45.311492Z","id":"6bb7a60b921f63965d0d93e4212b2c09aa1c7ed774018b9b028ceee91d63eb1e","body":{"detail":"No Docker engine was available when it was written. What was checked: the base images and cargo stage copy deploy/Dockerfile's; the binary it builds, under Bazel, starts on a scratch home and answers /v1/previews 401, 200, wrong_instance 403 and wire_skew 426 as deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md says. Not checked: that the root .dockerignore leaves everything clax-bot-workspace-service's dependencies include, that UID 10001 can write a bind-mounted home, and git 2.39 from bookworm against the commands crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs runs. The first docker build and one proposal settle these.","kind":"concern","summary":"service.Dockerfile has never been built, and nothing publishes its image","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:16:35.121112Z","id":"c7cbc962dde407d07b1c01d2cfb0d4c6052a7e800cac342fb6edf6e3b863c710","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker/src/workspace.rs reads the Worker secrets CLAX_WORKSPACE_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID and CLAX_WORKSPACE_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET (front_headers, read in crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs) and outgoing sends them as CF-Access-Client-Id and CF-Access-Client-Secret on every request, beside the bearer. Both or neither: one alone is Setup::Unusable, so the panel says failed. deploy-lib.mjs workspaceFrontPlan keeps them out of the record, uploads them when given in the environment, and refuses them on a preview. deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md 'The tunnel' and docs/prod.md 'ClaxBot's workspace service' now make Access with a Service Auth policy and Protect with Access the default. The fake service in crates/clax-worker/fake-workspace.mjs refuses a request without the headers as Access would. Nothing has run against a real tunnel or Access application. .github/workflows/staging.yml does not pass the two secrets to deploy.mjs yet.","kind":"comment","references":"cde8eb1121d3f61b2c5571ba863a9572b33459f800dc0bcf0a11a746657c5e8e","summary":"Option (a) is built, not yet run against real Access; the close is the owner's","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T00:30:28.135080Z","id":"479f51351324cb52a45373115acfacb6e36c022978208597440d4cddc12d86a1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3ca2d0b98341010e944b1d4cc2042b7a5175cf2c76c66bc7c6a57382c838c5d4","summary":"Default taken, for the owner to accept or change: preview_timeout_secs = 86400, the most a wait may be (MAX_PREVIEW_SECS, crates/clax-store/src/queue_repos.rs:100), with preview_poll_secs = 60. Deploys have taken 9.8 to 18.6 minutes and a person reads the change first. The wait sits in no run: propose answers at once and a detached task watches the preview (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs watch_preview), the ledger keeps it past the run's end (reap keeps an entry while awaiting.until is ahead) and a restart takes up what is left (take_up_wait). Over a day the Worker tends every 30 s (TEND_EVERY, crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs:81) while previews_until_ms is ahead: at most 2880 alarms and GET /v1/previews, however many fixes wait, with Kept saved at most once a minute (SAVE_EVERY_MS); the service makes 1440 looks at a preview per waiting fix. Those counts are read from the code, not measured. The queue's people now hear at the proposal (needs_person_in, crates/clax-store/src/queue_notifiers.rs), so the wait no longer has to end for anyone to be asked. A /preview later than a day still reaches nobody.","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:30:51.508019Z","id":"0c4147c9f930a21204ddcd6d2876e2563f18046b9727c1dddc8fa559a00e84b5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3ca2d0b98341010e944b1d4cc2042b7a5175cf2c76c66bc7c6a57382c838c5d4","summary":"A /preview later than the wait still reaches nobody by itself, and the stream now says so: Store::set_fix_preview_missed writes NoticeEvent::FixWaitEnded, whose message says a preview deployed from now on reaches nobody and that a member hands the fix over with its link (crates/clax-server/src/notifiers.rs fix_wait_ended). Test: api_queue_notifiers a_wait_that_ends_after_the_held_message_went_tells_the_stream_once.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T19:23:52.776682Z","id":"0b007aa7f80c0b95c220b010968879349432fa1f62c80568a71bdf982c1d9ce7","body":{"detail":"Measured in local Docker on 2026-11-07 (not Daytona), a model's cold run in clax-workspace:1 left 5 GB (a web fix) and 7.4 GB (a Rust crate's tests under //crates/clax-commands) in /home/clax/.cache, sampled with du every two minutes; the image is about 3.3 GB. Together about 10.8 GB against --disk 10. Memory is not the constraint: docker stats peaked at 5.28 and 5.47 GiB with about 16 cores and no limit; the cgroup's memory.peak read 7.53 GB because it counts reclaimable file cache. With --cpu 4, Bazel runs fewer compiles at once. Options: ask Daytona to raise the organization's disk limit and push the snapshot with a larger --disk; keep 10 and watch the first live run's disk (a run that fills it fails its build, not the host); or point Bazel's output somewhere the snapshot's disk does not count. Settled with record 8ab1456e's live run (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":82},"content_hash":"035b10e5f4259a0c22802b7db696ed187f83cc438717dd51dbe24f24a167e664"},"summary":"A cold run's ~/.cache and the image together may not fit the snapshot's 10 GB disk, the most an organization gets unless Daytona raises it","tags":["status:needs-decision","deploy","daytona","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T19:23:52.776744Z","id":"7a1e5a84cf03dd9370952c6334c9725fdf8a214792ec353c162fa1c6e9682199","body":{"detail":"protected_paths covers the store's sign-in and authorization files (secrets, roles, visibility, grants, people, passkeys) but not these: credits.rs keeps ClaxBot's spend and credit lifts, sessions.rs and routes/sessions.rs keep browser sessions, and bot_web.rs keeps the bot's web fetch settings. A change to them still passes a person's review and the /preview gate, so this is a question of how much review leans on. Protecting them narrows what ClaxBot may fix. To decide: add any of them to protected_paths, with allow lines in deploy/claxbot-workspace/path-cases.txt turned to refuse lines, checked by scripts/check-claxbot-paths.py.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"d7d24e077578b6222df0541af3cb9326b748203a0f21418934f70f34c6d9ba26"},"summary":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs, bot_web.rs and sessions.rs, and crates/clax-server/src/routes/sessions.rs, are writable by ClaxBot","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T19:23:52.777432Z","id":"09ed82a1b408d8ec628a446c57fbd0cfc2cdb6873c18a42c45c9b4172e8dd453","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cde8eb1121d3f61b2c5571ba863a9572b33459f800dc0bcf0a11a746657c5e8e","summary":"No longer holds: the Worker sends an Access service token on every request to the service, from the secrets CLAX_WORKSPACE_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID and CLAX_WORKSPACE_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET (docs/prod.md, \"ClaxBot's workspace service\", step 6; deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md, \"Put Access in front of it\"). Proposed for closing by whoever owns it.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T19:23:52.777849Z","id":"5ef78d6140350efa1e36c8dd7cc6ceba17c70be07f7e838f8cb068c7eee295c0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3ca2d0b98341010e944b1d4cc2042b7a5175cf2c76c66bc7c6a57382c838c5d4","summary":"No longer holds: deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml sets preview_timeout_secs = 86400, and a wait that ends unanswered tells the queue's members (comment 0c4147c9 on this thread). Proposed for closing by whoever owns it.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
